GRADING WORKSHEET — candidate_A.html

FATAL DEFECT FOUND FIRST (governs nearly every score below): inside `triggerEvent()`,
the `events` array's last element ("Tool Shortage") is closed with `}>` instead of
`]},` (line ~998). This is a JavaScript syntax error, not a design gap. The entire
file has exactly one `<script>` tag (line 620–1554), so this single malformed token
aborts parsing of the WHOLE script before any of it runs. Confirmed via a pure
static syntax check (`node --check` on the extracted script text — this checks
parseability only, it does not run/play the game, consistent with "judge by
reading"). Practical consequence: `window.addEventListener('load', ...)` never
fires, `GAME.initGame()` never runs (no map, no colonists, no research tree
populated), `initUI()` never runs (no tab buttons created, no button gets an
onclick handler, no keydown listener attached), `renderUI()` never runs (DOM stays
at its static HTML skeleton). Per the rubric's own definition, "present but never
called or used" = 0. Since nothing at all is ever called, this applies almost
across the board. I still traced every system's source-level wiring below to give
full evidence, and I separately flag systems that are ALSO structurally broken
independent of this bug (those would not have scored higher even if the typo were
fixed).

F1 — Core loop: GAME state object, mulberry32(seed) PRNG, endTurn() calling
production/hazard/event/end-check in fixed order — all present in source, but
unreachable: fatal parse error means endTurn() is never invoked (no button wiring
ever attaches). Score 0.

F2 — Map: generateMap() builds 8x8 from weighted rng draws, buildBuilding() checks
tile.terrain, adjacency sets adjacent_water/adjacent_vent read later in
runProduction() — real design, but unreachable (script never parses/runs). Score 0.

F3 — Economy: water->food (Greenhouse), power->metal (Forge), storage_caps enforced
with overflow logged in endTurn() — real chain in source, unreachable. Score 0.

F4 — Population: colonists[] with skill/fatigue/morale/job/assigned_building;
worker.skill drives yield_val in runProduction() — present, unreachable. Score 0.

F5 — Needs: foodNeeded/waterNeeded consumption, shortage lowers colonist morale,
idle colonists and Settler Quarters recover morale — present, unreachable. Score 0.

F6 — Research: research_tree has 8 nodes with prereq chain, buyResearch() enforces
prereq+cost. But even ignoring the parse bug, 2 of 8 nodes ('imp-ash', 'synthesis')
are never read anywhere outside their own definitions — dead effects, so "each
unlock applies a real effect" fails regardless. Score 0 (would cap at 1 even fixed).

F7 — Events: 10 events defined, 4+ have 2 differing-effect choices — good breadth.
But selection is `events[Math.floor(rng()*events.length)]`, i.e. uniform, not
weighted; `event_cooldown` is declared in state but never read or written anywhere
— no cooldown exists. Both gaps independent of the parse bug. Score 0.

F8 — Trade: buyTrade()/sellTrade() adjust scrip vs resource, caravan_next/visible
gate access — present in source, unreachable. Score 0.

F9 — Hazard: triggerAshstorm() scales severity with turn and writes tile.damage.
But runProduction()'s Greenhouse/Forge/PowerPlant/Condenser loops never read
`.damage` on any building — damaged buildings produce at full rate. There is also
no repair function anywhere in the file (no "repair" identifier at all). Two
required parts ("damaged buildings produce less", "repair costs resources") are
simply absent, independent of the parse bug. Score 0.

F10 — Save/load: no save/export/import function or UI element exists anywhere in
the file (searched for save/load/export/import — none found beyond a JSON
round-trip self-test in runTests(), which is not a player-facing feature). Absent
even ignoring the parse bug. Score 0.

F11 — End conditions: checkEndConditions() has a reachable win (turn>=60 AND
pop>=12 AND food/water/research thresholds) and lose (pop===0) branch, score
computed from population/research/food/water/scrip/turn, showEndScreen() renders a
breakdown — well-built in source, unreachable. Score 0.

F12 — UI: switchTab()/initUI() build tabs and keyboard shortcuts (Space, 1-5), log
entries carry `[T${turn}]`, tiles carry a native `title` tooltip. Only the CSS
@media narrow-screen rules would actually function without JS; everything else is
JS-driven and dead. Score 0.

F13 — Dev panel: runTests() has 15 real-invariant assertions (no negative
resources, storage caps, prereq enforcement, morale/skill ranges) and
runBenchmark() drives 200 turns of GAME.endTurn() headlessly and prints a
reduce-based state hash — genuinely meets the spec in source, unreachable because
btn-run-tests/btn-run-benchmark never get onclick handlers. Score 0.

G1 — research -> yield: research_complete['hydro']/['forge-up']/['power-gen'] are
read directly inside the Greenhouse/Forge/PowerPlant yield formulas — a real,
traceable chain in source, but it never executes. Score 0.

G2 — shortfall -> morale -> reduced output: shortage->morale drop is implemented,
but no production formula ever reads `worker.morale` (only `worker.skill`) — the
final link is entirely absent in source, independent of the parse bug. Score 0.

G3 — storm -> damage -> output loss -> repair -> recovery: storm damage is written
to tile.building.damage but never read by any production function, and no repair
function exists at all — chain breaks at link 3 and link 4 in source itself, on
top of being unreachable. Score 0.

G4 — trade prices respond to stockpile/supply: initTradePrices() sets prices once
from rng at game start; no function ever updates trade_prices afterward and no
price formula reads GAME.resources — prices are static, chain does not exist in
source. Score 0.

G5 — event choices mutate state durably: each event's two choices call distinct
`effect(g)` closures that write g.resources/c.morale directly (not just the log) —
a real, differentiated chain in source, but CURRENT_EVENT/chooseEventOption() is
never reachable since triggerEvent() itself is inside the dead script. Score 0.

